   If you point a tool at the simulator and then at a real console, test it
   on the simulator first, back up the real console before any change, and
   check the result on the console itself.

5. Beta, support and updates

   The software is a beta. It may be changed, have features removed, or stop
   being published at any time. Verbose Software has no duty to support,
   maintain or update it.

   The software contacts the internet only for these: once a day at start-up
   (unless turned off) and when asked, it reads the release list of its
   GitHub repository, sending its version number; when the user installs an
   update, it downloads the installer from there; and when the user fetches
   weather on the bench, it sends the ZIP code and the location and date to
   the weather services named in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. System Snapshots
   and other data the user loads stay on the user's computer.

